sition":"1785857801217614001-79b801c6-eb25-4cce-ab10-f9d2eb5a7eb9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785857607042405001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `rebar-brainstorm` skill (`examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md`) documents the\npre-implementation design protocol, including a section on authoring tickets to pass the\nplan-review gate and reviewing only unblocked tickets. However, it does not state that a\n**blocked ticket is a successful terminal state** of the review cycle, nor does it warn against\nusing `rebar review-plan --force` to bypass the claimability fast-fail. A recent real drift\n(session log `5eb0`, epic `708d`) showed an agent rationalizing repeated `--force` reviews of\nblocked tickets from a vague human instruction — each individually plausible, collectively\ndefeating the gate. This is a documentation-only reinforcement to close that guidance gap.\n\n## Approach\n\nAmend the existing \"Before recording tickets, read the project's plan-review gate\" section of\n`SKILL.md` with an explicit, positively-stated policy paragraph (already drafted and staged in\nthe working tree; this ticket lands it through Gerrit):\n\n1. State that a blocked / not-yet-claimable ticket (status `closed`/`idea`/`blocked`, or `open`\n   but blocked by an unclosed dependency) has **already completed the review cycle successfully**\n   for the current cycle — the gate's fast-fail is the intended outcome, requires no further\n   agent action, and the ticket re-enters the queue on its own via `rebar ready` when its\n   blockers close.\n2. Prohibit `review-plan --force` as an agent move: it is a human-operator escape hatch; a vague\n   or implied instruction is not authorization to force but at most a reason to ask a single\n   clarifying question (naming the block and the risk). Include the rationale (a forced review\n   mints a signed attestation against non-final dependencies that silently goes stale) and the\n   \"do not treat a series of individually-plausible forces as collectively acceptable\" warning.\n\nRationale: authoring the reinforcement as a positive policy (mirroring the skill's existing\nprose style and the `docs/plan-review-gate.md` semantics) is the lowest-risk way to prevent\nrecurrence, and keeps the guidance single-sourced in the skill that agents load for this\nworkflow. No code paths, tests, or gate behavior change — this only documents existing,\nalready-enforced runtime behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md` — add the blocked-ticket-is-done +\n  no-`--force` reinforcement paragraphs to the plan-review section. Documentation only.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Documentation-only change; no automated test tier applies (no code, no behavioral oracle).\n- Verification is by inspection: the plan-review section of `SKILL.md` contains the two new\n  directives with the stated semantics, and the surrounding section still reads coherently\n  (no duplicated or contradictory guidance about `rebar ready` / dependency-order review).\n- `make lint` is not applicable to a Markdown skill asset; no lint/build/test target covers it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md` states that a blocked / not-yet-claimable\n  ticket has completed the review cycle successfully for the current cycle and needs no further\n  agent action until `rebar ready` resurfaces it; verified by reading the plan-review section.\n- [ ] The same section explicitly prohibits `rebar review-plan --force` as an agent move, frames\n  it as a human-operator-only escape hatch, and directs the agent to ask a single clarifying\n  question instead of inferring authorization; verified by reading the section.\n- [ ] The change is documentation-only (no edits outside `SKILL.md`) and the section remains\n  internally consistent with the existing `rebar ready` / dependency-order guidance; verified by\n  the Gerrit diff touching only that one file.\n- [ ] The change lands via Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` (a `rebar-ticket`\n  trailer + DCO sign-off on the commit).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md","reason":"add blocked-ticket-is-done + no review-plan --force reinforcement paragraphs to the plan-review section (documentation only)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e9351153-68d2-4c4a-ad02-df8ca082e903","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"72ab-4e0b-ada4-4919","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reinforce blocked-ticket + no --force policy in rebar-brainstorm skill","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["358863b4-fd26-4d46-aaa0-debd47ca7b62","6ca0df5d-81ab-4c92-9756-07d42ce8f0ae","6819bb8a-53f2-40da-9a4e-2533b0d8428b","e9351153-68d2-4c4a-ad02-df8ca082e903","79b801c6-eb25-4cce-ab10-f9d2eb5a7eb9"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785857801217614002,"uuid":"7bd4313b-b019-447e-b231-fad957c3f347"}